The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
retval = tty_ldisc_lock(tty, 5 * HZ);
if (!tty->ldisc)
    retval = tty_ldisc_reinit(tty, tty->termios.c_line);
```
Reason:
Holding the line discipline lock during the `tty_reopen()` process, even when a line discipline is already present, can interrupt ongoing I/O operations. This unnecessary locking mechanism can lead to user-visible disruptions, such as interrupting a login process when a user enters a long password.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
ld = tty_ldisc_ref_wait(tty);
if (ld) {
    tty_ldisc_deref(ld);
} else {
    retval = tty_ldisc_lock(tty, 5 * HZ);
    if (!tty->ldisc)
        retval = tty_ldisc_reinit(tty, tty->termios.c_line);
}
```
Reason:
The patch optimizes the `tty_reopen()` function by first checking if a line discipline is present and only locking it if necessary. This prevents the interruption of ongoing I/O operations, thereby fixing the user-visible issue and improving performance by avoiding unnecessary locking when a line discipline is already in place.

